---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { DISCORD_INVITE_LINK } from "../lib/links";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About the Computer Technology Society of Newfoundland Labrador."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">
      About CTS-NL
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none mt-8">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        The Computer Technology Society Newfoundland Labrador, better known as
        CTS-NL or simply CTS, is a community for anyone who works in or is
        curious about software, technology, and computing in Newfoundland and
        Labrador.
      </p>

      <p>
        Every Thursday, we get together for <strong>Project Night</strong>. It is
        an informal evening for making progress on a project, talking through a
        problem, or catching up with people who share your interests.
      </p>

      <p>
        Everyone is welcome, regardless of race, culture, politics, sexual
        orientation, gender, gender variance, or nationality. The group is not
        specifically aimed at youth, but young people interested in computer
        technology are welcome too.
      </p>

      <p>
        CTS-NL is for people rather than businesses, though we are happy to work
        with and support local companies. Members help one another develop
        technical skills, manage projects, and learn the things that come up
        along the way. You do not need a particular job title or level of
        experience to take part.
      </p>

      <h2>History</h2>
      <p>
        CTS-NL began after a 2014 CodeNL talk prompted a conversation about the
        lack of a developer community in the province. A few alumni of Memorial
        University's Computer Science Society decided to start one. During its
        first year, the group met at different coffee shops and bars every two
        or three weeks.
      </p>

      <p>
        We settled on Jumping Bean Coffee on Elizabeth Avenue and started a
        weekly Project Night there in early 2016. Meetings continued for years,
        paused during COVID, and resumed in 2022. We have used a few other venues
        since then, including Element Bar &amp; Lounge before it closed and the
        QEII Library during winters when Jumping Bean closed early. Jumping Bean
        remains our usual home.
      </p>

      <h2>Get involved</h2>
      <p>
        Most conversations happen on <a href={DISCORD_INVITE_LINK}>Discord</a>.
        Join whenever you like, introduce yourself if you feel like it, and drop
        by a Thursday meetup when it suits you. It is also perfectly fine to
        read along until you are comfortable joining in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
